  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Every stem is two short statements with the same who and two different actions. Never mix two different people in one stem.",
      "The correct choice keeps that who once and joins both action phrases with and.",
      "Wrong choices must stay readable kid sentences. Do not invent nonsense letter strings.",
      "Tier 1 distractors put and in the wrong spot or scramble the word order.",
      "Tier 2 adds a dropped-verb choice or a choice that joins things instead of actions.",
      "Tier 3 uses a near miss that keeps both whos, such as The horse ran and the horse ate.",
      "Use <NAME> from names.txt. Never write a real name.",
      "Stay in kid world: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather. No brands."
    ]
  },
